  "hindi": "वे बच्चे की ओर स्त्रियों की तरह दौड़ पड़े; रथों की तरह पत्थर एक साथ आगे बढ़े। तुमने बहकर निकलने वालों को तृप्त किया, लहरों को दबाया; हे इन्द्र, तुमने रोकी गई नदियों को छोड़ दिया।",
  "english": "They ran forth toward the child like women; like chariots the stones went forth together. You satisfied the outflowing ones, you pressed down the waves; you, O Indra, released the rivers that were held back.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The subject of dadruḥ is not stated. adrayaḥ may be 'stones' (pressing-stones) or 'mountains'; 'stones' is used. visṛtaḥ is uncertain: acc. pl. 'outflowing ones' (taken) or nom. sg. 'released'. abhi is taken with garbham.",
